  "schema": 1,
  "about": "Single source of truth for component-level fault mapping, shared by the web twin and the landing film. Names are mesh-name prefixes from the exported GLBs (the same object names as the Blender assemblies). '{c}' is the faulted cylinder. 'pipeline' is ordered from where the fault originates to the sensor that reads it. 'evidence' lists the detector channels (backend/detect/calibration.py) that see the fault; an empty list means the fault is waveform-only and the scalar detector cannot see it by design (backend/runtime/registry.py). Validated by tests/test_component_map.py.",
  "highlight": {
    "fault_rgb": [1.0, 0.28, 0.05],
    "ghost_rgb": [0.06, 0.22, 0.38],
    "evidence_rgb": [0.35, 0.9, 0.95],
    "note": "Fault and ghost colours are the values of M_Fault_RedHighlight and M_GhostVision_XRay in apps/blender_twin/standalone_fault_diagnostic_app.py, so Blender and web show the same thing."
  },
